From: baristahaus <baristahaus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:23:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(ops): decide the fused HyperConnection route before
 allocating its workspace

fused_mix allocated its staging, partials and square sums (about 25.7 KB a
token) before launch_fused_mix found that the device cannot host the
cooperative grid, then returned false with those buffers still held. The
general route that follows is sized by
hyperconnection_mix_workspace_capacity_bytes, which does not include them,
so on a device below 160 SMs (GB10: 48 SMs give 54 columns a CTA against
the 16 the Up tile allows) the op test runs out of workspace
(std::bad_alloc in finish_mix). fused_mix now checks fused_mix_grid() first.
Devices that take the fused route are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PB8TNZ3p817zVAp6aH4yrz
---
 src/ops/launcher/hyperconnection.cu | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ops/launcher/hyperconnection.cu b/src/ops/launcher/hyperconnection.cu
index dfaae9c0..669a0e19 100644
--- a/src/ops/launcher/hyperconnection.cu
+++ b/src/ops/launcher/hyperconnection.cu
@@ -1038,7 +1038,11 @@ bool fused_mix(Tensor& hyper, const Tensor* previous_block_output,
                Tensor& block_input, Tensor* injection, WorkspaceArena& workspace,
                cudaStream_t stream, const HyperConnectionActivation* activation) {
     const int tokens = hyper.ne[1];
-    if (tokens > kFusedMaxTokens || (activation != nullptr && activation->capture != nullptr)) {
+    // Decide before allocating: a device that cannot host the cooperative grid (fewer than 160
+    // SMs, e.g. GB10's 48) takes the general route, whose workspace capacity does not include
+    // these buffers.
+    if (tokens > kFusedMaxTokens || (activation != nullptr && activation->capture != nullptr) ||
+        fused_mix_grid() == 0) {
         return false;
     }
     Tensor staged      = workspace.alloc(DType::BF16, {kHyper, tokens});
